course: dictionary
lesson: 5487
title: Words for materials
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a material, something you can pour, stretch or make things from. Latex is one of them. The words around it give you clues. «Balloons are made by dipping balloon-shaped formers in liquid latex» tells you latex is a liquid you can dip things into before it hardens.
explain: The sentence also says latex is «the sap of rubber trees». Sap is a sticky liquid inside a plant, so latex must be a liquid that comes from plants. Test it: swap in «the sticky liquid of rubber trees» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Latex can also mean the rubbery material made from that liquid. Look at the words near it: gloves, paint and balloons all tell you the meaning is the stretchy material, not the liquid. Words like «latex allergy» show that people can react to it, so you know it is a real thing people touch.
fact: Latex means a white, milky liquid from some plants, especially the rubber tree.
fact: Latex is also a rubbery material made from that liquid, or made artificially.
fact: Rubber trees are tapped for latex in places like Malaysia and Brazil.
fact: Latex gloves are used by doctors and dentists.
fact: Some people have a latex allergy, so schools may avoid latex balloons.
exercise: «Balloons are made by dipping balloon-shaped formers in liquid latex.» What is latex in this sentence? | A gas that makes balloons float | *A white, milky liquid from plants such as the rubber tree | A small type of balloon | A dry powder made from sand
exercise: «...the sap of rubber trees» tells you where latex comes from. What does sap mean here? | *A sticky liquid inside a plant | A bright light | A kind of tree bark | A hard metal used for tools
exercise: Doctors wear «latex gloves». Which word near latex tells you it is a material used to make things? | doctors | wear | *gloves | the
test: Which place is named as one where rubber trees are tapped for latex? | *Malaysia | Iceland | Antarctica | Greenland
test: Why might a school avoid latex balloons? | Because they are the wrong colour | Because they always pop in the sun | *Because some people have a latex allergy | Because they are too heavy to lift
exam: What does latex mean? | A bright light | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of cloud | *A milky liquid from plants, or a rubbery material made from it
